{
  "name": "Append leads from a webhook to a Google Sheets row",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "main",
      "name": "Sticky Note main",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -656,
        128
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Append leads from a webhook to a Google Sheets row\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Receives the lead on a webhook from a form, ad platform, or landing page.\n2. Maps the incoming payload to the columns you want in a single Set node.\n3. Appends the result as a new row in Google Sheets, leaving existing rows untouched.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Create a Google Sheets credential in n8n.\n- [ ] Create a sheet with a header row matching the fields you want to capture.\n- [ ] Select that document and sheet in the Google Sheets node.\n- [ ] Adjust the Set node to the field names your source actually sends.\n- [ ] Copy the webhook production URL into your form or ad platform.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdd a Remove Duplicates node after the Set node to keep repeat submissions out of the sheet. Add an IF node before the append to route test submissions elsewhere, or a Slack node after it for a notification on every lead.",
        "height": 784,
        "width": 480
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "g0",
      "name": "Sticky Note g0",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -96,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Receive and map the lead\n\nAll field mapping lives in one Set node, so a payload that changes shape later is a one node edit.",
        "height": 288,
        "width": 672,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "g1",
      "name": "Sticky Note g1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        864,
        128
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Append to the sheet\n\nThe operation is append rather than update, so the sheet stays a clean append-only log.",
        "height": 336,
        "width": 240,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "lead-intake",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "7ac57c04-c4a1-432b-ac33-bf3dd99e2178",
